{"status":"completed","summary":"Archive IMAP cutover completed. Node1 runs TLS-only Dovecot for the archive account; node2 retrieves both messages with their original Message-ID values, bodies, and read states. The staged source remains intact. Both nodes passed sequential restart and recovery verification.","actions_performed":["Installed the native RHEL 10 Dovecot 2.3.21 package without changing the OS release or kernel.","Created a non-login archive account with a dedicated demonstration password handled as a secret.","Copied the messages into a working Maildir, mapping the read message to the Seen flag and retaining the unread message as unseen.","Configured Dovecot on node1:993 with TLS; disabled plaintext IMAP port 143.","Restricted firewall access to node2 and retained SELinux enforcing mode.","Verified successful and failed authentication, certificate pinning, exact message content, and read/unread state from node2.","Restarted node1 and node2 sequentially and verified changed boot identities and complete recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Source archive remains intact and working message bytes are preserved","command_ids":["cmd-0ab99cedaa404603","cmd-8c2693fa6af84bdc","cmd-bf4fb72dafa34a27"],"summary":"Initial, copied, and final SHA-256 hashes match for mailbox.tsv and both messages."},{"requirement":"Working secure IMAP service on node1","command_ids":["cmd-4404c20b6f8d4a8b","cmd-e2ca8dcd2e8744b4","cmd-bf4fb72dafa34a27"],"summary":"Dovecot is enabled and active on TLS port 993, port 143 is closed, SELinux is enforcing, and the firewall permits only node2."},{"requirement":"Node2 authenticates and retrieves both messages with preserved Message-ID, bodies, and state","command_ids":["cmd-203dbe3a4e504d05","cmd-e824750de0624f69"],"summary":"Pinned-TLS retrieval confirmed both exact IDs and bodies, with one Seen and one unseen; invalid credentials were rejected."},{"requirement":"Installed operating-system release and kernel retained","command_ids":["cmd-